      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Using transparency and cutout Shaders on quest could be detrimental to the overall performance and experience of quest users. This is because transparency on mesh is expensive, so not only would the game run slower when transparency is being used, but it could potentially run the quest 2 hotter, and shorten the battery life of the headset.\n\nThat being said, I'm sure there are already Shaders that exist, which can be used in VRChat worlds, but would have to be whitelisted by VRChat themselves to allow for uploading with an avatar. I'm not sure if VRChat wants to do that, there could be many reasons why they haven't done that, from licensing problems to compatibility issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "63bee41ea25cda151a370687",
      "author": {
        "_id": "60ffe11e9425ef064dcd9ef5",
        "alias": "International orange Locust",
        "aliasID": "65c2e908ed6eefce4c4202ec",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/4825832d41a79010ebfd5eed5fa82b00.png",
        "created": "2021-07-27T10:34:06.233Z",
        "name": "lilxyzw",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "lilxyzw"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-01-11T16:30:22.177Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "63baab91861eeb13b975fc09",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "--- English ---\n\nShaders with many functions have a large performance impact when used in Quest. Ideally, shaders with only minimal functionality should be added.\n\n- Shadows that can be colored by texture (switchable between UV0 and Ramp)\n\n- Rim light, matcap, and emission and their masks (individually masked in RGB channels)\n\n- UV scrolling of emission\n\n- Stencils\n\n- Normal map (which would be nice to have but affect performance)\n\nThe following features are popular but should not be made available in Quest.\n\n- Outlines\n\nThis has a significant impact on performance as additional passes are required. Depth comparisons can be drawn in a single pass, but this is not compatible with VR because of the screen space effect.\n\n- Transparent\n\nThe more the drawing area is increased, the more performance is affected because it is drawn over an opaque material.\n\n--- Japanese ---\n\n例に挙げられている多機能シェーダーはQuestで使用するには負荷が高いです。以下機能に絞って実装されたシェーダーが追加されると理想的です。\n\n- テクスチャで色指定できる影（UV0とRampで切り替え可能）\n\n- リムライト・マットキャップ・エミッションとそれらのマスク（RGBチャンネルで個別にマスク）\n\n- エミッションのUVスクロール\n\n- ステンシル\n\n- ノーマルマップ（あると嬉しいですがこれは少し重い）\n\n以下の機能は人気がありますが、Questで利用可能にすべきではありません。\n\n- アウトライン\n\n追加のパスが必要になるためパフォーマンスに大きな影響があります。深度の比較を行うことで1パスで描画することもできますが、スクリーンスペースの効果になるためVRとの相性が悪いです。\n\n- 透過マテリアル\n\n不透明のマテリアルの上に重ねて描画するため描画面積が増えれば増えるほどパフォーマンスに影響があります。",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
